# Service logs must be useful (hard rule)

Operator principle (Phil, 2026-08-21):

> **When logging is filled with garbage entries with no security or
> operational usefulness, the log value is near worthless.**

## The rule

> **Default Settings → Service logs (`/settings/service-logs`) is an
> operator stream. It carries security-relevant actions (NIST AU-2 / AU-3)
> and real operational state changes or failures only. Successful polls,
> heartbeats, empty ticks, IF NOT EXISTS / already-exists-skipping
> notices, and debug chatter must not appear at the default level.**

## Default stream

| May appear at `info`+ | Must not appear by default |
| --- | --- |
| Startup / shutdown / drain (`service.started` / `.stopping` / `.stopped`) | `sqlx::postgres::notice` / `already exists, skipping` |
| Real state change (one line, before → after) | Successful Hyper-V / Docker / inventory polls |
| Security-relevant mutate, authz deny, secret/custody events | “polled N VMs / N containers, ok”, empty list, “no work” |
| Failures (`warn` / `error` + recovery) | Catalog already loaded, schema IF NOT EXISTS, websocket ping |

Default filter is **not debug**. Do not invent product env vars for this
([`no-environment-variables.mdc`](no-environment-variables.mdc)). Use the
shipping `EnvFilter` (`sqlx::postgres::notice=off`) and `debug!` / `trace!`
or no log for ignore-safe polls.

## Three live streams (quiet each)

Settings → Service logs has **three** tail types. A prior pass that only
quieted stderr is incomplete. Apply the same default-stream bar to every
emit path and to the tail display filter:

| Stream | On-disk file | Emit path |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **stderr** | `service-stderr.log` | SCM-captured tracing (shipping `EnvFilter`) |
| **rolling** | `pim-offline-server.log` | Same tracing filter, pim-diag JSON file |
| **stdout** | `service-stdout.log` | SCM stdout pipe (usually empty; still rotate/archive) |

`/settings/syslog` is a forwarding settings page, not a fourth tail.

Display chatter filter (`service_log_view::filter_operator_chatter`) runs
on all three tails unless the operator chooses Debug or Trace.

## Archive and policy (not chrome-only)

Competitor default (CyberArk / Delinea / BeyondTrust / Windows Event Viewer):
keep N days and/or max size, **rotate into a ZIP archive** (never a silent
drop), list and download prior archives, delete only with confirm (and/or
automatic retention) — both recorded (AU-2 / AU-3).

| Key | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `SERVICE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS` | Age before rotate / archive scavenge |
| `SERVICE_LOG_ARCHIVE_ENABLED` | Rotate into ZIP; when false, skip auto-rotate (no silent drop) |
| `SERVICE_LOG_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB` | Size trigger for rotate |
| `SERVICE_LOG_MAX_ARCHIVES` | Cap; oldest removed with an audit / `info` record |
| `SERVICE_LOG_DELETE_ALLOWED` | Operator delete after confirm; still audited |

Policy is `pim-app-config` / Settings API — never an environment variable.
Debug stays off by default; saving policy must not raise the default stream
to debug. Archives live beside the live files in
`pim_diag::daemon::server_log_dir()`.

## Hyper-V / Docker

- Successful poll with no change: **no log**.
- Appeared / disappeared / started / stopped / failed: **one** `info`
  line naming the guest and before → after. Never dump the inventory.
- Controller / spawn failures: `warn` / `error` + recovery
  ([`silent-failure-is-a-bug.mdc`](silent-failure-is-a-bug.mdc)).

## Forbidden

- Default `info` on OK polls, ticks, or IF NOT EXISTS DDL
- Dropping real errors to hide noise
- Claiming Service logs “quiet” while the live page is still a wall of skip/poll/notice
- Quiet only one of the three streams
- Archive / retention / delete chrome that does not persist or rotate
- Silent purge of live files or archives

